ing to the morpho\u0002logical appearance of the cells]). Obligately an\u0002aerobic, sporeforming, small, slightly curved,\nL1313@P12: gram-positive rods occurring in pairs or short\nL1314@P12: chains (Fig. 11). The oval, nearly terminal\nL1315@P12: spores were rarely seen. Heat-resistant cells\nL1316@P12: were most often demonstrated from a 3-week\u0002old CM slant culture inoculated into maltose\nL1317@P12: broth which was then heated at 80 C for 10\nL1318@P12: min. From PY-glucose broth cultures, cells\nL1319@P12: were about 0.6 to 0.8 pm wide and 1.3 to 2.8\nL1320@P12: pm long.\nL1321@P12: Colonies. After incubation for 5 days in\nL1322@P12: RGCA roll tubes, subsurface colonies were 0.2\nL1323@P12: to 0.5 mm in diameter, white, and lenticular to\nL1324@P12: raspberry shaped. Some colonies were of such\nL1325@P12: indefinite form that there was doubt that the\nL1326@P12-13: A6-31, A10-29A, All-17, R3-13, R8-47B, S6F-46, VOL. 26, zyxwvutsrqp\nL1327@P13: 1976 zyxwvutsrqpon\nL1328@P13: EMENDATION OF zyxwBACTEROZDACEAE 251\nL1329@P13: FIG. 11. Clostridium leptum ATCC zyxwvut29065. Top,\nL1330@P13: Cells from PY-fructose broth culture. Bottom, Spore\nL1331@P13: from CM slant.\nL1332@P13: area picked (under x 10 magnification) truly\nL1333@P13: contained a colony. Surface colonies on BHIA-S\nL1334@P13: roll streak tubes were minute to 0.5 mm in\nL1335@P13: diameter, circular, entire, low convex, tan, and\nL1336@P13: translucent. Only 2 of 11 strains tested grew on\nL1337@P13: the surface of BAP incubated anaerobically. No\nL1338@P13: hemolysis was detected. No reaction was noted\nL1339@P13: with the 5 of 11 strains that grew on the surface\nL1340@P13: of EYA.\nL1341@P13: Cultural characteristics. Broth cultures\nL1342@P13: showed smooth to stringy sediment, usually\nL1343@P13: without turbidity. Growth was markedly stim\u0002ulated by the presence of some carbohydrates\nL1344@P13: (Table 3), even though the pH of the medium\nL1345@P13: was not appreciably lowered in t